Terminal output optimization

- Minimize terminal output to reduce context/token consumption.
- For Maven, use "mvn -q -B -ntp" by default.
- For builds, tests, and other verbose commands, capture output to a temporary log.
- On success, report only a short status summary.
- On failure, show the last 80 relevant lines.
- Preserve original command exit codes.
- Read additional log content only when necessary for debugging.
- Never discard diagnostic information permanently before it can be inspected.